    "rotation_name": "Soybean → Corn + Brachiaria intercrop",
    "message_to_farmer": "Seu João, in the last five years the rains on your farm started later and ended earlier, and the soil stayed bare from July to October, right when the first heavy storms arrive. You care most about water and soil, so we suggest keeping soybean and safrinha corn but sowing brachiaria together with the corn. After the corn harvest the grass keeps the ground covered, holds moisture, reduces erosion and leaves straw for planting soybean in October. Your income should stay close to today. Please talk to a local agronomist before deciding."
